WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.173
Allow 4 minutes.

00:00:01.413 --> 00:00:03.333
A review can be practical and brief.

00:00:03.573 --> 00:00:05.195
Start with the work requirement.

00:00:05.435 --> 00:00:10.789
Read each objective, find its practice, and identify the evidence that would show success.

00:00:11.029 --> 00:00:13.931
Flag a gap when the assessment cannot support the claim.

00:00:14.171 --> 00:00:19.269
Use Bloom’s language to explain the mismatch, not to rank people or decorate slides.

00:00:19.959 --> 00:00:24.973
Worked example: a manager requests a 20-minute change module for ticket triage.

00:00:25.213 --> 00:00:27.858
Requirement: use the new rule card correctly.

00:00:28.098 --> 00:00:31.789
Draft A has six definition screens and a terminology quiz.

00:00:32.029 --> 00:00:39.069
Draft B has a brief rule explanation, a worked example, two supported cases, a new-case check, and a job aid.

00:00:39.309 --> 00:00:40.994
Choose B for this requirement.

00:00:41.234 --> 00:00:44.285
Keep definitions only where they enable the decision.

00:00:44.525 --> 00:00:53.250
A rollout communication about why the process is changing may still be needed, but communication and demonstrated skill answer different questions.

00:00:53.940 --> 00:01:01.023
Review task, 60 seconds: sketch one objective, one practice task, and one assessment task for something you teach.

00:01:01.263 --> 00:01:04.036
Underline the same required action in all three.

00:01:04.276 --> 00:01:09.908
Note one tool or reference available during work that should also be available during practice.

00:01:10.598 --> 00:01:12.945
Finish by stating the limit of your evidence.

00:01:13.185 --> 00:01:17.899
Passing a short sample check supports a narrow conclusion about these decisions.

00:01:18.139 --> 00:01:22.662
It is not a professional credential or proof of full workplace proficiency.

00:01:23.352 --> 00:01:24.440
Now it's your turn.

00:01:24.680 --> 00:01:30.696
A sponsor says an 80% terminology score proves readiness to triage unfamiliar cases.

00:01:30.936 --> 00:01:32.152
What should you recommend?

00:01:32.392 --> 00:01:35.507
Pause the video and make your choice in the activity below.

